{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "Ten servants of the Almighty who fought the Desolations, then abandoned their oath at Aharietiam.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "The ten Heralds of the Almighty, worshipped across Roshar. Each is tied to one of the Ten Essences and one order of the Knights Radiant.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "epilogue" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": [],
  "history": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Changes to the Oathpact",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "120" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "77" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "99" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Honor expanded the Heralds' access to the Surges after Natanatan's destruction, while keeping them bound by oaths.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "120" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "When the nine abandoned Talenel, Ishar took their suffering onto himself. The Oathpact remained, but was damaged.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "77" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Chanarach's death at Shallan's hands returned her to Braize. She, rather than Talenel, broke and allowed the next Desolation.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "99" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "In Shinovar",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "6" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "33" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "110" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "140" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "144" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "postlude" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Dalinar sent Kaladin with Szeth to try to help Ishar.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "6" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ishar rejected Kaladin's offer of help and described carrying the other Heralds' pain.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "33" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "After confronting Kaladin, Nale acknowledged that he was as damaged as the other Heralds.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "110" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Kaladin's Fifth Ideal cleared Odium's corruption from Ishar, restoring his clarity.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "140" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Kaladin replaced Jezrien in a renewed Oathpact that protected the spren and bound Retribution.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "144" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Heralds returned bodily to Braize but sheltered their minds in a vision of Ashyn.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "postlude" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "mechanics": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Heraldic life and power",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "64" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "108" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "93" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "88" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "145" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "147" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Vedel used Regrowth and their Connection to Honor to hold their bodies and souls at a fixed age.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "64" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Their immortality is related to the Oathpact but does not depend on it.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "108" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Heralds can enter a vision through a Connection to someone inside it.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "93" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Limited access to Fortune can guide a Herald toward where they are needed.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "88" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Their bodies are formed from Investiture according to how they see themselves, rather than taken from other people.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "145" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Oaths between Roshar's Shards help bind the Heralds to the system.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "147" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Abilities",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Their Surgebinding doesn't depend on their Honorblades.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Each Herald holds an Honorblade, which grants two Surges.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "16" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A raysium dagger can trap a Herald's soul in a gemstone.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "121" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "92" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "parts": []
    },
    {
      "title": "History",
      "items": [],
      "parts": [
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Before the Oathpact",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "107" },
                { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "64" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Jezrien led Odium's empire on Ashyn, while Nale served its opponents. The future Heralds fled the devastated world through Ishar's elsegate.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "107" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Vedel made the new Heralds ageless through their Connection to Honor.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "64" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "The Desolations",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "38" },
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "47" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "After each Desolation the Heralds return to Braize, where they are tortured until one breaks and the Desolation begins again.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "38" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Spren copy the Heralds' powers, making the first Surgebinders. Ishar organises them into the Knights Radiant, and each Herald becomes patron of an order.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "47" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "The Last Desolation",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "42" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "At Aharietiam, every Herald but Taln abandons the Oathpact and leaves their Honorblade.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "They tell people the Desolations are over.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "42" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Era of Solitude",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "119" },
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prologue" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "121" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Taln is tortured alone on Braize for four and a half thousand years. The other nine hide among the people of Roshar.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "119" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "They go mad: Nale grows compassionless, Kalak paranoid, Jezrien drinks, and Shalash destroys her own art.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prologue" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "121" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "The True Desolation",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "epilogue" },
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "76" }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "121" },
                    { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "93" }
                  ]
                },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "121" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "82" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "111" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Taln returns to Kholinar and warns that the Desolation has come.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "epilogue" },
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "76" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Moash kills Jezrien with a raysium knife, trapping his soul.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "121" },
                    { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "93" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Shalash finds Taln at Thaylen Field.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "121" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Ishar, ruling Tukar, refuses to join Dalinar's coalition.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "121" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Shallan finds that Restares, leader of the Sons of Honor, is Kalak.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "82" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Ishar fights Dalinar's Windrunners and flees.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "111" }]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
